    "explanation_html": "<section class=\"dtos-explanation\" aria-label=\"Custom DTOS personal assessment\"><h3>Custom DTOS personal assessment</h3><p class=\"tw-final-verdict\">WORTH PURSUING</p><section class=\"tw-decision\" aria-label=\"Trade decision summary\"><section class=\"tw-decision-lead\" aria-label=\"Decision and next step\"><p>Why this decision: Rebuild fit: you give up current production while gaining meaningful priced future capital. Reserve coverage and pick-range uncertainty remain explicit.</p><p>Next step: Preview the exact offer, review both teams\u2019 costs and confirm the other manager\u2019s motivation.</p></section><section class=\"tw-decision-market\" aria-label=\"Current Market comparison\"><h4>Current Market</h4><div class=\"tw-market-caption\"><span>You send <b>250</b></span><span>You receive <b>250</b></span></div><div class=\"tw-market-bar\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Current Market totals are equal.\"><span class=\"neutral\" style=\"flex-basis:50.000%\"></span><span class=\"neutral\" style=\"flex-basis:50.000%\"></span></div><p>Current Market totals are equal.</p><small>Current values, not trade-date grades. Market advantage is separate from strategy and lineup impact.</small></section><p>Conditional current-week optimal legal-lineup cost (Season 2026, week 2): 4.00 projected points. This prepared comparison does not establish dependable availability or replacement cover; review the roster limitations.</p><p>Rebuild fit: you give up current production while gaining meaningful priced future capital. Reserve coverage and pick-range uncertainty remain explicit.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Cost and uncertainty: Neutral DTOS: WORTH PURSUING. Neutral Market cost remains separate. Optimal legal-lineup production falls 4.00 points per supported week; Useful legal-replacement production falls 1.00 points per supported week</p><p>Your team: Conditional Season 2026, week 2 optimal-lineup change -4.00 projected points.</p><p>Conditional average across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: -4.00 projected points per week; not a season forecast.</p><p>Neutral Market: 250 sent / 250 received; this is value compensation, not acceptance evidence.</p><p>Useful replacement production changes -1.00 points per supported week.</p><p>Season 2026, week 2 reserve cover: before 6.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots); after 5.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots).</p><p>Conditional week 2 reserve-production change: -1.00 points; not an injury forecast or a second starting lineup.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Player availability is uncertain; usable replacement production is provisional.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Projection source freshness is qualified; these are conditional projections, not guaranteed production.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Original projection observations are not confirmed Fresh; replacement production remains conditional.</p><p>Other weekly reserve effects and coverage gaps are listed separately in Before and after \u00b7 both optimal lineups.</p><p>Personal Custom future-capital value: 0 sent / 250 received. Picks do not supply projected points; future outcomes are uncertain.</p><p>Their team: Conditional Season 2026, week 2 optimal-lineup change +2.00 projected points.</p><p>Conditional average across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: +2.00 projected points per week; not a season forecast.</p><p>Neutral Market: 250 sent / 250 received; this is value compensation, not acceptance evidence.</p><p>Useful replacement production changes +4.00 points per supported week.</p><p>Season 2026, week 2 reserve cover: before 4.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots); after 8.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots).</p><p>Conditional week 2 reserve-production change: +4.00 points; not an injury forecast or a second starting lineup.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Player availability is uncertain; usable replacement production is provisional.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Projection source freshness is qualified; these are conditional projections, not guaranteed production.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Original projection observations are not confirmed Fresh; replacement production remains conditional.</p><p>Other weekly reserve effects and coverage gaps are listed separately in Before and after \u00b7 both optimal lineups.</p><p>Future capital Market value: 250 sent / 0 received. Picks do not supply projected points; future outcomes are uncertain.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Their recorded direction is WIN NOW; it does not prove willingness to accept this offer.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Market fairness and receiving a pick do not establish rebuilding intent or predict acceptance.</p><p>Review both teams\u2019 sacrifices and discuss the stated compensation and direction with the other manager; this is not a prediction of acceptance.</p><p>Other team: Win-now fit: this costs future flexibility, and materially improves the optimal legal lineup. Any reserve loss remains a disclosed cost.</p><p>Their cost and uncertainty: Spends 250 Market units of future capital</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Evidence limit: Projection evidence is Unavailable; retained numerical evidence is provisional, not freshly verified.</p><p>Inspect the main drawback, edit or reevaluate this trade.</p><details class=\"tw-player-facts\"><summary>Player production, projections and rank definitions</summary><section><h4>a</h4><p>QB \u00b7 NFL team unavailable \u00b7 Age 31.0 \u00b7 Unknown</p><p>Listed position eligibility: QB. Availability and roster rules are assessed separately in the legal lineup.</p><p>Market positional rank: QB3 \u00b7 Priced rostered players in the selected league.</p><p>Current Market: 250.</p><p>Sleeper projection: 10.00 \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Week 2 \u00b7 Unavailable.</p><p>Sleeper actual production: Unavailable points per completed-week score observation \u00b7 Unknown observations \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Sel